Subject: [PATCH 2237/3799] soh: rename func_80B0BE20 -> EnSw_SetSurfaceBasis

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: rotates the stored tangent onto a new floor poly's normal, rebuilds the orthonormal basis and reads the actor's rotation back out of it
Defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Sw/z_en_sw.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Sw/z_en_sw.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Sw/z_en_sw.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Sw/z_en_sw.c
index 48cbe29ca..b294e54af 100644
--- a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Sw/z_en_sw.c
+++ b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Sw/z_en_sw.c
@@ -71,7 +71,8 @@ void EnSw_CrossProduct(Vec3f* a, Vec3f* b, Vec3f* dst) {
     dst->z = (a->x * b->y) - (a->y * b->x);
 }
 
-s32 func_80B0BE20(EnSw* this, CollisionPoly* poly) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80B0BE20: rotates the stored tangent onto a new floor poly's normal, rebuilds the orthonormal basis and reads the actor's rotation back out of it
+s32 EnSw_SetSurfaceBasis(EnSw* this, CollisionPoly* poly) {
     Vec3f sp44;
     Vec3f sp38;
     f32 sp34;
@@ -166,13 +167,13 @@ s32 func_80B0C0CC(EnSw* this, PlayState* play, s32 arg2) {
         temp_v0_2 = func_80B0C020(play, &sp84, &sp78, &sp9C, &sp6C);
